    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "0b6b7819e1bd5f1652b3e9066a7473c6c4439c84",
            "parents": [
                "533d49096d1f45e8389f2349aef2b655945add52"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/37/82437/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                "username": "robert-ercean"
            },
            "createdOn": 1753917357,
            "author": {
                "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                "username": "robert-ercean"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Instead, add some details of what is Darwin.  \"A network switch ...\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                        "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                        "username": "robert-ercean"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this upstream?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                        "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                        "username": "robert-ercean"
                    },
                    "message": "No, the custom DBUS server is kept downstream.\nThe Darwin BMC is not directly connected to the chassis EEPROM, so it gets the x86's Serial Number some other way (through the console). \nWe have to create a custom server that reads this serial number and then exposes it through the same interface as FruDevice."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                        "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                        "username": "robert-ercean"
                    },
                    "message": "@spinler@us.ibm.com\n\nThe DBUS server is currently waiting for review and will be available on our downstream repo: https://github.com/facebook/openbmc/tree/helium/meta-facebook"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                        "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                        "username": "robert-ercean"
                    },
                    "message": "@spinler@us.ibm.com Hey Matt, just following up on your previous question."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "It sounds like this system won't work with upstream openbmc code, so I'm not sure why you need to even put this config in upstream openbmc?\n\nI will defer to @patrick@stwcx.xyz since he's a meta and upstream openbmc maintainer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Let's drop this entire line from the commit message.\n\nDarwin is a [network switch] system we already have in production using a non-OpenBMC implementation.  Robert is an intern working on a proof-of-concept of running OpenBMC natively.\n\nPart of this effort is to figure out what code changes need to happen to support a new platform.  Part of this effort is to figure out where we messed up the hardware design (and the EEPROM is one of them obviously).\n\nIf we end up having multiple of these platforms, or this becomes a longer-term endeavor, I think we'll do what HPE did and figure out a way to get the EEPROM data exposed via contributed daemon.\n\nThis is a pretty minimal config and generally we want to have as much of our code upstreamed as possible.  I think there is pretty light burden in having this merged.  It also helps with the \"figure out what code changes need to happen to support a new platform\" for our network switch team."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/darwin_chassis.json",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "You can always hardcode the FBPN."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/darwin_chassis.json",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marco Kawajiri",
                        "email": "kawajirimarco@googlemail.com",
                        "username": "kawmarco"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Jagpal, the FBPN is not consistent across all darwin devices, it's fine to keep this as \"N/A\" IMO"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/darwin_chassis.json",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please follow up with a new commit for the FBPN if we decide to fill one in."
                }
            ],
